{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patchset 2 (Gerrit 2185) addresses the LLM-Review -1:\n- BLOCKING bugfix-size-attestation: earned a signed, file_impact-SCOPED plan-review attestation (verdict PASS, no blocking findings; currency_basis=file_impact so it survives unrelated HEAD movement).\n- Advisory 2 (error-handling): fetch_coordination_lock is now BOUNDED — non-blocking fast path, jittered poll to _FETCH_COORD_WAIT_S=30s, then degrade to unlocked with a warning (CAS retry is the net). No longer pins the long-lived MCP server behind a wedged peer fetch.\n- Advisory 3 (tests): CAS-exhausted snapshot test now asserts the EXACT bounded budget (== resolve_stall_attempts) instead of >=2.\n- Advisory 4 (tests): added coverage for the lock's best-effort fallbacks — non-git dir (common dir None), os.open OSError, and the bounded-wait degrade when a peer wedges the flock.\n- Advisory 1 (maintainability): documented on is_ref_cas_mismatch that CAS is a strict subset of is_git_lock and callers must test CAS first (the fetch paths do).\nGates green in-worktree: lint, typecheck, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0, 12/12 in the new suite."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787569337457368001,"uuid":"f65bbcd6-947f-45bc-97aa-2d879734ded4"}